 "reading": "On the unseen block the offset model misses the block's level. The frozen candidate-size offset predicts the four fitted caps with RMSE 0.0321 (max 0.0432) and mean residual -0.0313, against a 16-tag leave-one-cell-out error of 0.0216 for the curve with free block offsets and 0.0184 for the size model itself. The 24 seed-by-cap values give RMSE 0.0592 (max 0.1153), inside the 16-tag seed LOO of 0.0747, so the per-seed scatter is no worse than at fitting time while the level is. The block sits below both fitted 16-tag blocks at all four caps \u2014 coverage 0.5797/0.6789/0.8096/0.8826 at caps 20/40/80/112 against 0.6362/0.7356/0.8299/0.9032 for current-16 \u2014 although its candidate space is the same size (63 edges per seed). Its mean log candidate size, 4.156258, is identical to fresh-16's, so the size model gives it fresh-16's offset (0.4128) and cannot tell the two blocks apart, yet the block still sits 0.0171 to 0.0369 below the fresh-16 bracket at every cap. Applying a known 16-tag offset instead is no better in kind: cell RMSE 0.0392 (current-16) and 0.0260 (fresh-16), both outside the fitted 16-tag LOO. Candidate size therefore replaces the block label inside the fitted blocks, but it does not predict a new block's offset; the cell error is outside the fitted 16-tag scale.",
